course: dictionary
lesson: 7860
title: Raiders: sudden attacks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A raider is a person who makes a sudden attack on a place, usually to steal things or cause damage. The word comes from a raid, which is a quick, surprise attack. «Viking raiders» sailed in boats to attack towns and monasteries.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The Great Wall was built against horse-riding raiders from the north.» A wall is built to keep something out, so raiders must be attackers who come from outside.
explain: A raider can also be a robber. «Ram raiders» crash a car into a shop and grab what they can. In sport, raiders are the players who make quick attacks. Check the context to see which meaning fits.
fact: A raider is a person who makes a sudden attack on a place.
fact: Raiders often want to steal things or cause damage.
fact: «Viking raiders» came by boat to attack towns and monasteries.
fact: The Great Wall is many walls, built over 2,000 years, to keep out horse-riding raiders from the north.
fact: In sport, raiders are attackers who make quick, surprise attacks.
exercise: What is a raider? | A kind helper who brings food | A teacher who marks homework | *A person who makes a sudden attack on a place
exercise: In «ram raiders crash a car into a shop», what are the ram raiders most likely doing? | Delivering a parcel | Singing a song | Painting a fence | *Breaking into a shop
exercise: In «The Great Wall was built against horse-riding raiders from the north», what was the wall guarding against? | Trees | *Attacks from raiders | Tourists | Rain and snow
test: Which phrase means a robber who crashes a car into a shop? | Fridge raider | *Ram raider | Steppe raider | Viking raider
test: In the joke phrase «fridge raider», what is the raider doing? | Fixing the fridge | Painting the fridge | *Sneaking snacks from the fridge | Building a fridge
exam: Which meaning fits raider in «The Cossacks fought Tatar raiders on the steppe»? | A player on a sports team | *An attacker who makes a sudden raid on a place | A robber in a shop | A kind neighbour
